Why Logging?
Production scripts must always generate logs.

Without logs:
Problem occurred
No idea where

With logs:
Easy troubleshooting
Root Cause Analysis
Write Logs
echo "Backup Started"

Store in File:
echo "Backup Started" >> backup.log
Logging with Timestamp
echo "$(date) Backup Started" >> backup.log

Example:
Sun Jun 14 10:00:00 Backup Started
Production Logging Function
log() {
    echo "$(date) : $1" >> /var/log/devops.log
}

Usage:
log "Deployment Started"
log "Docker Container Created"
log "Deployment Completed"
Capture Errors
command >> output.log 2>&1

Explanation:

1 = Standard Output

2 = Standard Error

>&1 = Combine Both
Production Deployment Example
#!/bin/bash

LOGFILE="/var/log/deployment.log"

echo "$(date) Deployment Started" >> $LOGFILE

docker pull myapp:latest >> $LOGFILE 2>&1

docker stop myapp >> $LOGFILE 2>&1

docker run -d myapp:latest >> $LOGFILE 2>&1

echo "$(date) Deployment Completed" >> $LOGFILE
